[10.7949, "o", "◆ explored · listed .\r\n▸ $ python -m pytest tests/ -v\r\n"]
[10.9416, "o", "  └ exit 127 · 3 lines\r\n"]
[12.3798, "o", "▸ $ python3 -m pytest tests/ -v\r\n"]
[15.0007, "o", "  └ exit 1 · 39 lines\r\n"]
[38.2548, "o", "◆ explored · read discounts.py, test_discounts.py\r\n▸ edit shop/discounts.py\r\n"]
[38.3500, "o", "  └ edited shop/discounts.py (1 replacement)\r\n"]
[39.5446, "o", "▸ $ python3 -m pytest tests/ -v\r\n"]
[41.6190, "o", "  └ exit 0 · 17 lines\r\n"]
[44.4095, "o", "\r\n"]
[44.6004, "o", "The discount tests were failing because the BULK discount logic had two issues:\r\n"]
[45.2531, "o", "1. It used `total > BULK_MINIMUM` (strictly greater) instead of `total >= BULK_MINIMUM` (greater or equal), so the discount didn't apply at the minimum threshold of 5000 cents.\r\n"]
[45.6977, "o", "2. It returned `int(total * RATES[code])` (the discount amount) instead of `int(total * (1 - RATES[code]))` (the price after discount).\r\n\r\n"]
[46.1896, "o", "I fixed both by changing the condition to `>=` and applying the discount correctly. All tests now pass.\r\n\r\n"]
[46.3004, "o", "Changed file: shop/discounts.py\r\n"]
